{"id": "225dc3a0-8571-4191-85c3-86f6a3d39a4e", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The skill shows up in my skills list but skill_read isn't working on it, and it's absent from the capability_map entirely—not marked as directly available or accessible via Context Gatherer. I'm trying to figure out whether this static skill is meant for me to use at all, or if it's meant for some other purpose I'm not seeing yet.

This makes sense now — the capability map explicitly says CloudTrail-related questions must always be delegated to Context Gatherer regardless of size, and this skill is likely a remote/custom skill accessible to it but not to me directly. Since this question is clearly about CloudTrail coverage, I should delegate it to gather_context rather than trying to handle it myself.

"}]}

{"id": "b5f36a70-d1c2-4615-a586-05b6a6f5e675", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "This is exactly the kind of CloudTrail coverage question that needs a closer look at your trail configuration — let me dig into that for you.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_JigFwc936Pir4wsVj8r5CM", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Audit CloudTrail coverage for this member account. Determine (1) which trail(s) apply to this account, specifically identifying any organization trail (isOrganizationTrail=true) versus account-level trails, and what coverage the org trail contributes (management events, data events, regions, multi-region scope) versus what it does NOT cover; and (2) whether CloudTrail Event history alone (the default 90-day event history, no trail required) is sufficient for audit purposes, or whether a configured trail is required, and why.",
  "context": "User is in a member account of an AWS organization and wants to understand: which part of their CloudTrail coverage comes from the organization trail, and whether their auditors can rely on Event history instead of a trail. This is a coverage/configuration audit question, not a question about finding who performed a specific action.",
  "resources": ["CloudTrail trails in this account (describe_trails, get_trail_status, get_event_selectors for each trail)", "account 012345678901_1", "region us-east-1 (check is_multi_region_trail / home region)"],
  "timeframe": "current configuration state, not historical",
  "criteria": "Identify: 1) any trail with isOrganizationTrail=true and what account-level trails (if any) also exist; 2) the event selectors/advanced event selectors on the org trail (management events, data events for S3/Lambda/DynamoDB etc, read/write types); 3) whether it is multi-region; 4) explicit comparison of Event history limitations (90-day retention, management events only, no data events, not exportable long-term, no near-real-time alerting) versus a trail's capabilities, to give a clear audit-readiness verdict."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit CloudTrail trail configuration and org trail coverage in this account"}], "created_at": null}
